        <item>
         <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="about_pictures_layout">
          <property name="spacing">
           <number>6</number>
          </property>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_pictures_title_label">
            <property name="font">
             <font>
              <bold>true</bold>
             </font>
            </property>
            <property name="text">
             <string>About the pictures</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_pictures_label">
            <property name="text">
             <string>&lt;b&gt;Group level and cohort level&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• At the group level, each report file is a group. Its pictures show the subjects of the report.&lt;br/&gt;• At the cohort level, the report files with the same group label in step 2, "Group Definition", are put together. The colors differentiate the groups.&lt;br/&gt;• On every picture, the sleep stages are differentiated by the line style.&lt;br/&gt;• You can generate one picture for each channel or ROI, or put them all on a single picture.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sleep stages and section&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Select the preferred sleep stages and the section to display, "Total", a sleep cycle, a clock hour or a stage hour.&lt;br/&gt;• "All" plots the power of all the stages together.&lt;br/&gt;• Some reports are computed on annotations instead of sleep stages (step "Section Selection" of "Analyze EEG Spectral Power"). For these reports, the annotations are plotted in place of the sleep stages, and the sleep stage selection is not used.&lt;br/&gt;• A run cannot mix reports computed per sleep stage and reports computed on annotations. Mixing them stops the run with an error.&lt;br/&gt;• The section must be in the reports. Check the distributions you need in the step "Output Files" of "Analyze EEG Spectral Power".&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Picture names&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• At the group level, a picture is named with the report file name, the channel or ROI label, the section and the stages, then _mean or _mean_std with "MEAN" or "MEAN + STD". For example, learn-nsrr01_PSA_report_EEG_psa_Total_All_mean_std.pdf.&lt;br/&gt;• "One picture per group" adds avg, for example learn-nsrr01_PSA_report_avg_psa_Total_All_mean_std.pdf for several channels.&lt;br/&gt;• At the cohort level, a picture is named cohort_psa, then the display option and the section, and the channel or ROI label for one picture per channel. For example, cohort_psa_mean_std_Total.pdf and cohort_psa_mean_std_Total_EEG.pdf.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="textFormat">
             <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
             <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
            <property name="variant" stdset="0">
             <string notr="true">help</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
         </layout>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </widget>
